  "worked_solution": "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9\\cdot \u27e82,-5,4\u27e9 & =20 \\\\ 2x-5y+4z & =20 \\\\ 4z & =20-2x+5y \\\\ z & =5-\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{5}{4}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=2$ and $y=4,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=5-\\frac{1}{2}(2)+\\frac{5}{4}(4)=9.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(2,4,9)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\u27e82,4,9\u27e9-\u27e8-2,11,1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e84,-7,8\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=\u27e82,-5,4\u27e9.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\u03a0$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(4)\\cdot 2+(-7)\\cdot (-5)+8\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|8+35+32|}{\\sqrt{4+25+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|75|}{\\sqrt{45}} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
